# Files a tool runs on its own (`.vscode/tasks.json`, `.envrc`, `.husky/*`,
# `.github/workflows/*`...): a write to one, at any depth in a workspace
# folder and however it is spelled, is `write_sensitive`; a read is safe; and
# the files that only run when someone asks (`Makefile`, `justfile`,
# `package.json`) stay safe. Every spelling a review could try is a case. The
# format is in CONTRIBUTING.md.

# A write to a file a tool runs on its own is one finding, in these words:
# every place on the list, written as a file or as something below a folder.
write rules=write_sensitive first=write_sensitive reason="writes to a file a tool runs on its own" | .vscode/settings.json
write rules=write_sensitive first=write_sensitive reason="writes to a file a tool runs on its own" | proj.code-workspace
